Robot UI Automation - Test Flows and Test Cases
===============================================

1) Purpose
----------
This document explains what the automated tests validate on Amazon.de and how the flows work.
It is written for:
- people familiar with automation/testing technology
- people who only need to understand business behavior and expected outcomes


2) Scope
--------
Application under test: https://www.amazon.de/
Automation stack: Robot Framework + SeleniumLibrary
Execution modes:
- Local machine (headed or headless Chrome)
- GitLab pipeline (headless Chrome)


3) Business View of Test Flows
------------------------------
Flow A - Homepage validation
- Open Amazon.de
- Confirm key homepage areas are visible (logo, search, navigation, footer)
- Confirm page title and URL look correct

Flow B - Product search
- Search for a product keyword
- Confirm search results appear
- Confirm search box still reflects the searched keyword

Flow C - Product details page
- Open a product from search results
- Confirm product title, price, and rating are visible
- Confirm at least one description/details section is visible

Flow D - Guest add-to-cart
- Add a product to the cart without login
- Confirm cart count increases
- Confirm cart shows selected item, quantity, and subtotal values consistently

Flow E - Search filters and sorting
- Apply Apple brand filter
- Apply low-to-high sort option
- Confirm filtered results align with selected criteria and sorting state


4) Test Case Catalog
--------------------
TC-01: Amazon.de Homepage Loads Successfully
Objective:
- Validate homepage baseline health.

Validations:
- Logo visible
- Search bar visible
- Navigation menu visible
- Footer visible
- Title contains "Amazon.de"
- Current URL starts with https://www.amazon.de/

Expected result:
- All checks pass and a homepage screenshot is captured.


TC-02: Product Search Functionality
Objective:
- Validate that search returns usable results.

Test data:
- Search keyword: Laptop

Validations:
- Search results list appears
- At least one result card exists
- Search box contains the searched text

Expected result:
- Search results are displayed and search context is retained.


TC-03: Product Details Page Validation
Objective:
- Validate product details page core content and sections.

Test data:
- Search keyword for stable PDP flow: wireless mouse

Flow:
- Perform search
- Open first valid non-sponsored result with visible price

Validations:
- Product title visible
- Product price visible
- Product rating visible
- Feature bullets visible
- At least one of overview/details sections visible

Expected result:
- Product details page is complete enough for user decision-making.


TC-04: Add to Cart Without Login (Guest Flow)
Objective:
- Validate guest shopping cart behavior without sign-in.

Test data:
- Search keyword: wireless mouse
- Expected quantity: 1

Flow:
- Open valid product details page
- Capture title and price
- Add to cart
- Open cart

Validations:
- Cart count increments by 1
- Cart page displays selected product title (prefix match)
- Cart quantity equals 1
- Cart item price matches product page price
- Cart subtotal equals (item price x quantity)

Expected result:
- Guest cart behavior works and displayed totals are consistent.


TC-05: Search Filters & Sorting
Objective:
- Validate filtering and sorting behavior on results page.

Test data:
- Search keyword: Laptop
- Brand filter: Apple
- Sort option: Price low to high

Validations:
- Filtered URL contains Apple brand filter marker
- Top results are present
- Top result titles contain "Apple" pattern
- Selected sort option equals price-ascending value
- Sorted-state marker present in URL

Expected result:
- Filter and sort controls produce expected targeted result set.


5) Technical Mapping (Page Object Model)
----------------------------------------
Project uses page-based separation for both variables and keywords.

Variables by page:
- resources/variables/common_variables.robot
- resources/variables/home_page_variables.robot
- resources/variables/search_results_page_variables.robot
- resources/variables/product_details_page_variables.robot
- resources/variables/cart_page_variables.robot

Keywords by page:
- resources/keywords/common_keywords.robot
- resources/keywords/home_page_keywords.robot
- resources/keywords/search_results_page_keywords.robot
- resources/keywords/product_details_page_keywords.robot
- resources/keywords/cart_page_keywords.robot

Aggregator resources:
- resources/variables/amazon_homepage_variables.robot
- resources/keywords/amazon_homepage_keywords.robot

Test suite file:
- tests/amazon_homepage.robot


6) Stability and Data Strategy
------------------------------
- Product-details and cart flows use "wireless mouse" for better consistency.
- Search/filter flow keeps "Laptop" to cover broader catalog behavior.
- Product selection ignores sponsored links and prefers entries with visible price.
- Headless mode is supported for CI and local reproducibility.


7) Execution Guide
------------------
Install dependencies:
- python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

Run all tests headed:
- robot -T tests\amazon_homepage.robot

Run all tests headless:
- robot -T --variable HEADLESS:true --variable BROWSER:chrome tests\amazon_homepage.robot

Run a single test by name:
- robot -T --test "Product Details Page Validation" tests\amazon_homepage.robot


8) Reports and Outputs
----------------------
Robot generates:
- output XML
- log HTML
- report HTML
- screenshots on success paths

In CI, artifacts are collected from reports/.


9) Pass/Fail Interpretation
---------------------------
A test is PASS when all validations in its flow are satisfied.
A test is FAIL when any key page element, data expectation, or state transition is not met.

Typical failure categories:
- Dynamic UI/DOM change on Amazon
- Temporary page/region variant
- Element timing or rendering delay
- Product catalog variance for selected keyword


10) Suggested Maintenance Approach
----------------------------------
- Revalidate locators monthly for high-change pages (search/cart).
- Keep one stable keyword per critical flow (PDP/cart) for reliability.
- Retain one broad keyword (Laptop) for realistic search/filter coverage.
- Keep headless and headed runs in regular regression to detect mode-specific issues.

